      "dom_id": "question-52149",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "If  $f(x)={x}^{2}+2x-1$ and $g(x)={x}^{2}-x+1,$ then $f(x)+g(x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We put a plus sign between the two polynomials, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)+g(x) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x-1)+({x}^{2}-x+1) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-1+{x}^{2}-x+1 & = \\\\ (1+1){x}^{2}+(2-1)x+(-1+1) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
