      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $f(y)={y}^{4}+3{y}^{2}-1$ and $g(y)=2{y}^{2}-3,$ write $f(y)+g(y)$ in **standard form**.\n\n$f(y)+g(y)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We put a plus sign between the two polynomials, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y)+g(y) & = \\\\ ({y}^{4}+3{y}^{2}-1)+(2{y}^{2}-3) & = \\\\ {y}^{4}+3{y}^{2}-1+2{y}^{2}-3 & = \\\\ {y}^{4}+(3+2){y}^{2}+(-1-3) & = \\\\ {y}^{4}+5{y}^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
